# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file the build context is
# the whole working tree - several GB of target directories, the unpacked
# test-build binaries, and any local .env. All of it is uploaded to the
# daemon, and whatever the COPY takes ends up in a layer that ships.
#
# Secrets first: .env is gitignored, so it exists locally and only locally.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output. `**/` is required, NOT decoration: Docker anchors ignore
# patterns at the context root, so a bare `target/` matches only the top one
# and leaves wasm/target and gui/src-tauri/target in the context - together
# well over a gigabyte, uploaded to the daemon and copied into a layer on
# every build. This is the one place the syntax differs from .gitignore.
**/target/
/target-win
/target-linux
/target-msvc
/target-gui
/target-cuda
/dist
/test-build

# Generated Tauri artifacts and the embedded sidecar binary.
gui/src-tauri/gen/
gui/src-tauri/binaries/

.git
.github
node_modules/
